From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0146: blueline screenshots (bluesnap=) and scripted touches
 (bluetouchscript=)

Lets the test loop see and drive iOS with nobody at the phone.

bluesnap=T,sb+T,... takes box-filtered copies of the panel memory
(1080x2160 BGRA; default 2x, RGB565 = 540x1080, 1139 KiB) at the given
times, bluesnap_on_reboot=1 one more right before bluereboot resets. They
go to the 128 MiB of userdata right below the console log area, through
the log's own UFS path, after checking that the HFS+ root volume ends
before it; an area header (count, used blocks, boot nonce) is reset when
armed. tools/phonetest.sh pulls them in recovery and tools/snap2png.py
makes PNGs.

bluetouchscript=TIME:ACTION,...;... injects taps, long presses and swipes
in panel pixels through sweet_hid_touch's mapping (edge flag included),
presses keys, starts a fake-accelerometer turn (volchord) or takes a
snap. Real touches are dropped while a touch step runs.

TIME is seconds after the UFS driver started (as bluereboot_after=N), or
sb+N: N seconds after SpringBoard first exists.

